const e="mid-south-fair-youth-talent-contest",u=2026,t="Built from the 2026 terms and rules (4 pages). It prints no entry fee amount, no contest venue, no judging criteria and no dates other than the fair opening date and the schedule mailing time. A contact e-mail address is printed but is not copied; the office street address is kept as a Variable. Scholarship amounts are mentioned only as a total.",n={Title:"Rules & Criteria",Subtitle:"Mid-South Fair Youth Talent Contest 2026: Junior and Senior divisions for young amateur entertainers.",NoticeTitle:"Please Read Before Registering",Notice:"Acts over the time limit are disqualified: 4 minutes in the Senior Division and 3 minutes in the Junior Division.",Notes:["Read the terms and contest rules carefully before entering.","Questions go to the Youth Talent Office: {{YouthTalentContact}}."],Sections:[{Key:"general",Title:"General",Items:["The contest discovers, develops and encourages young amateur entertainers from the eight-state area served by the Mid-South Fair.","Contestants can compete for {{PrizeTotal}}.","Vocal, dance and variety groups are divided into small groups (2-3 performers) and large groups (4 or more performers).","Accompaniment: recorded accompaniment must be on a single-track USB thumb or jump drive. The only track on the drive is the performance track. A drive with more than one track can be disqualified. Bring a second copy (backup) to check-in.","Props must be inanimate, except those used by a magician.","Acts using machetes, knives or any other item judged to be a weapon are not accepted.","Contestants may not use fire, smoke or any smoke effect on stage.","Contestants may enter and leave the stage only by the officially designated stage left and stage right. No act may enter or exit from the front (audience side) or from backstage.","Accompanists may be on stage but must not take visual importance in the act. They are not acknowledged individually and do not bow with the contestants.","Judges are told to consider whether the material is suitable. Presentations should be tasteful and right for the contestant's age and for a family entertainment venue.","The Mid-South Fair is not responsible for equipment, costumes or other belongings left at the fair before, during or after the contest.","Individual scores are posted for one hour after each round of the Senior Division. A parent or teacher observer is present at each contest to check which acts advance to the semifinal and final and who takes the top 4 places. No scores are mailed after the contest.","No individual scores are posted or released for the Junior Division."]},{Key:"eligibility",Title:"Who can enter",Items:["Senior Division: ages 13-21 on {{OpeningDate}}, the opening date of the Mid-South Fair.","Senior Division entry is by invitation: the first-place overall winner of a sanctioned preliminary contest, a finalist from the previous year's Grand Finals (if still eligible), or a special invitation from a Mid-South Fair representative approved by the Youth Talent Committee and given by the Youth Talent Director.","If the first-place winner of a preliminary contest is not eligible or already has an invitation, the Fair alone decides which act receives the invitation.","Junior Division: ages 9-12 on {{OpeningDate}}. The Junior Division is limited to the first 200 applicants.","No contestant under 9 years old may compete as a soloist or in a group.","No solo performer may compete outside their age group. No member of a group may compete in a lower age category.","A group with members from both age groups (Senior and Junior) must register in the Senior Division. For example, a group with one 13-year-old and two 12-year-olds must compete in the Senior Division.","All persons who take visual importance in an act must meet all qualifications: the age limit of the division, be listed on the application (Junior Division), and be invited or accepted by application as part of the act (Senior Division).","A contestant may compete as a soloist and separately as a member of a small group (2-3 members), but may enter only once as a soloist and once as a member of a small group. A member of a large group (4 or more) has no limit on the number of group acts.","No member of a Grand Final winning act may compete again in the same category.","The contest is for amateurs. A professional entertainer is one who earns more than one-half of their normal living expenses by performing in any category of the contest, is a union member, or has signed a contract with a professional agent or manager who is paid a salary or commission to find work in entertainment.","An entertainer who sings or performs on a record released for commercial distribution through normal retail outlets is a professional. Self-producing a record for friends and associates, for church group activities or as a demo does not count.","Professional status in one category makes the contestant ineligible for all categories. For example, a professional dancer may not compete as an amateur singer or musician.","An entertainer who wants to give up professional standing may apply to the Youth Talent Contest for a declaration of amateur standing. Each request is reviewed individually and the decision of the Youth Talent Contest Committee is final."]},{Key:"registration",Title:"How to enter",Items:["For the Senior Division, the act must stay the same as performed in the preliminary contest that earned the invitation, or as on the accepted application.","For the Junior Division, the act must stay the same as on the application.","No Senior Division group may add anyone after receiving an invitation without re-qualifying or getting approval from the Youth Talent Office.","If a group member was not part of the preliminary contest that earned the invitation, the act must re-qualify or apply and be invited as a completely new act.","Members of an act may drop out without penalty, unless this changes the act from a group to a solo.","Confirm your entry category at check-in. An act that appears on stage in a category different from its invitation or approved application is disqualified.","Competition schedules are mailed or e-mailed from {{ScheduleDate}}. No scheduling information is given by phone.","Only extreme scheduling conflicts are considered. Requests are accepted only in writing, by U.S. Mail or e-mail to the Youth Talent Office: {{YouthTalentContact}}.","To withdraw, call or write before the Monday of the week the fair begins. The fair always begins on a Thursday. Entry fees and tickets are not refunded."]},{Key:"levels",Title:"Rounds",Items:["Contests include Preliminary, Semifinal and Grand Final rounds.","The top 4 finishers of the Grand Finals are named (Grand Award, First, Second and Third Sweepstakes)."]},{Key:"fees",Title:"Fees",Items:["The rules print no entry fee amount. They state that entry fees and tickets are not refunded after withdrawal."]},{Key:"dates",Title:"Dates",Items:["The Mid-South Fair opens on {{OpeningDate}}.","Age is counted on the opening date of the fair.","Competition schedules are sent out from {{ScheduleDate}}."]},{Key:"venue",Title:"Venue",Items:["The Youth Talent Office is at {{YouthTalentOffice}}. The rules do not print the contest stage venue."]},{Key:"prizes",Title:"Prizes",Items:["Senior Division (ages 13-21): each act in the Grand Finals receives $50.00 and a Finalist's trophy.","Senior Division Grand Finals winners receive a trophy cup and cash: Third Sweepstakes Winner $500.00, Second Sweepstakes Winner $750.00, First Sweepstakes Winner $1,500.00 and Grand Award Winner $2,500.00.","The Senior Grand Award winner also returns the next year as special entertainment at the Youth Talent Contest Grand Finals.","Junior Division (ages 9-12) winners receive cash: Third Sweepstakes Winner $150.00, Second Sweepstakes Winner $250.00, First Sweepstakes Winner $500.00 and Grand Award Winner $750.00.","The Junior Grand Award winner performs as special entertainment at the Senior Grand Finals and returns the next year as special entertainment at the Junior Grand Finals."]},{Key:"conduct",Title:"Conduct",Items:["The Youth Talent Policy Committee does not accept offensive conduct by participants, teachers, parents or associates. Such conduct can lead to expulsion from the current and future editions of the contest.","Anything thrown off the stage at any time is cause for immediate disqualification.","Studio teachers are responsible for the control of parents and contestants. A violation may put the contestant's eligibility at risk."]},{Key:"judging",Title:"Judging",Items:["Judges may not discuss contestants or acts with anyone except the judges' panel. Do not approach judges to ask for an explanation of a decision.","Anyone who tries to discuss an act with a judge before, during or after a contest is disqualified.","After the winners are announced, the decisions of the judges are final in all Preliminary, Semifinal and Grand Final competitions.","The rules print no judging criteria. They state that a variety act divides the total score between the acts performed.","The act is timed from the first vocal utterance, first instrumental note or first dance movement. Exit tags are not timed, but if you speak, sing or play you are timed. An official timekeeper is present at all contests."]},{Key:"complaints",Title:"Protests",Items:["A protest about a rule violation must be made before the winners are announced.","A contestant found to be a professional who wants reinstatement as an amateur must protest within ten days of being told of the decision. The petition goes to the Mid-South Fair Youth Talent Office and is reviewed by the Youth Talent Contest Committee."]}],Documents:[{Title:"2026 Youth Talent Contest terms and rules (PDF)",Url:"https://landerscenter.com/assets/doc/2026-MSFYT_Rules-8333f1e8dc.pdf"}]},o=[{ParticipantType:"Team",Source:"Terms: Groups; Contest Rules 4, 15, 16, 17",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Small groups have 2-3 performers; large groups have 4 or more.","Members of an act may drop out without penalty, unless it changes the act from a group to a solo.","A member who was not part of the preliminary contest that earned the invitation cannot join; the act must re-qualify or be invited as a new act."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Small groups have 2-3 performers; large groups have 4 or more.
- Members of an act may drop out without penalty, unless it changes the act from a group to a solo.
- A member who was not part of the preliminary contest that earned the invitation cannot join; the act must re-qualify or be invited as a new act.`}],a=[{AgeGroup:"Senior Ages 13-21 Solo",Source:"Contest Rules 7",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Each act is limited to four (4) minutes. An act over the limit is disqualified."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Each act is limited to four (4) minutes. An act over the limit is disqualified.`},{AgeGroup:"Senior Ages 13-21 Group",Source:"Contest Rules 7",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Each act is limited to four (4) minutes. An act over the limit is disqualified."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Each act is limited to four (4) minutes. An act over the limit is disqualified.`},{AgeGroup:"Junior Ages 9-12 Solo",Source:"Contest Rules 7",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Each act is limited to three (3) minutes. An act over the limit is disqualified."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Each act is limited to three (3) minutes. An act over the limit is disqualified.`},{AgeGroup:"Junior Ages 9-12 Group",Source:"Contest Rules 7",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Each act is limited to three (3) minutes. An act over the limit is disqualified."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Each act is limited to three (3) minutes. An act over the limit is disqualified.`}],i=[{Title:"Vocal",Source:"Contest Rules 13",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The act is timed from the first vocal utterance, even a spoken greeting before the music starts."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:["No vocal utterance of any kind on an accompaniment track, for example an 'oooo', a whistle, background singers, someone saying '1, 2, 3', or synthesizers."],Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- The act is timed from the first vocal utterance, even a spoken greeting before the music starts.

## Not allowed
- No vocal utterance of any kind on an accompaniment track, for example an 'oooo', a whistle, background singers, someone saying '1, 2, 3', or synthesizers.`},{Title:"Dance",Source:"Contest Rules 7 and 13",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The act is timed from the first movement."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:["No taps or tap-effect sounds on any recording provided."],Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- The act is timed from the first movement.

## Not allowed
- No taps or tap-effect sounds on any recording provided.`},{Title:"Variety",Source:"Contest Rules 5",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["A vocalist who accompanies themselves is a variety act.","A variety act divides the total score between the acts performed. A 'song and dance' act can earn up to 20 points for the song and 20 for the dance, a maximum of 40 points. A self-accompanied vocalist is scored 20 for the vocal and 20 for the instrument of the maximum 40 points."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- A vocalist who accompanies themselves is a variety act.
- A variety act divides the total score between the acts performed. A 'song and dance' act can earn up to 20 points for the song and 20 for the dance, a maximum of 40 points. A self-accompanied vocalist is scored 20 for the vocal and 20 for the instrument of the maximum 40 points.`},{Title:"Instrumental",Source:"Contest Rules 7 and 13",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Instrumentalists can only be accompanied by live or taped piano. In a piano solo, no accompaniment is allowed.","If an electronic keyboard is used, all sounds must be created live on stage.","Bands and instrumental groups may have no accompaniment. All sounds must be created live on stage.","The act is timed from the first note."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:["No pre-programmed music or sound."],Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Instrumentalists can only be accompanied by live or taped piano. In a piano solo, no accompaniment is allowed.
- If an electronic keyboard is used, all sounds must be created live on stage.
- Bands and instrumental groups may have no accompaniment. All sounds must be created live on stage.
- The act is timed from the first note.

## Not allowed
- No pre-programmed music or sound.`}],s=[],r=[{Key:"OpeningDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Mid-South Fair opening date (age check date)",Value:"2026-10-01",Source:"Contest Rules 1"},{Key:"ScheduleDate",Kind:"text",Label:"Schedules sent from",Value:"the 3rd week of September",Source:"Terms: Schedules"},{Key:"PrizeTotal",Kind:"prize",Label:"Cash, prizes and scholarships",Value:"over $20,000 in cash and prizes, plus over $5,000 in scholarships",Source:"Introduction"},{Key:"YouthTalentOffice",Kind:"address",Label:"Youth Talent Office",Value:{Name:"Mid-South Fair Youth Talent Office",Address:"2584 Hwy 51 South",City:"Hernando, MS 38632",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Terms: Scheduling Conflicts"},{Key:"YouthTalentContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Youth Talent contact for questions",Value:{Name:"Debbie Banan",Role:"Youth Talent Contest contact",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:""},Source:"Introduction"}],l=[{Claim:"Rules, eligibility, time limits, disqualification rules, protests and cash awards are taken from the organiser's 2026 Youth Talent Contest terms and rules.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Mid-South Fair Youth Talent Contest 2026 terms and rules",Url:"https://landerscenter.com/assets/doc/2026-MSFYT_Rules-8333f1e8dc.pdf"}],c={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:t,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:o,AgeGroups:a,Competitions:i,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:r,Evidence:l};export{a as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,i as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,n as Page,o as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,r as Variables,u as Year,c as default};
